# FrontDesk Core Architecture Rules

## Overview
FrontDesk is a unified messaging hub that consolidates multiple communication channels into a single interface. This file defines the core architectural patterns and rules that apply across ALL providers.

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

### Three-Layer Architecture
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         UI Layer (Widgets)              │
│    src/widgets/frontdesk/providers/     │
│    - Components, Views, Hooks           │
└─────────────────┬───────────────────────┘
                  │
┌─────────────────▼───────────────────────┐
│      State Layer (Recoil)               │
│    src/store/frontdesk/atoms/           │
│    - Atoms, Selectors                   │
└─────────────────┬───────────────────────┘
                  │
┌─────────────────▼───────────────────────┐
│      Service Layer (APIs)               │
│    src/services/frontdesk/              │
│    - REST APIs, WebSocket               │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

