## 🔌 Provider Pattern

### Standard Provider Structure
Every provider MUST follow this structure:

```
providers/{provider-name}/
├── {provider}-provider-view.tsx     # Main view/router
├── components/                      # Provider-specific components
│   ├── conversation-list/
│   ├── message-view/
│   └── compose/
├── hooks/                          # Custom hooks
│   ├── use-{provider}-provider.ts  # Main hook
│   └── use-{feature}.ts           # Feature hooks
├── utils/                          # Utilities
│   ├── filter-utils.ts
│   └── validation-utils.ts
└── types/                          # TypeScript types
    └── {provider}.types.ts
```

### Provider Registration
To add a new provider:

1. **Create provider structure** following the pattern above
2. **Add Recoil atoms** in `src/store/frontdesk/atoms/{provider}.atoms.ts`
3. **Create API service** in `src/services/frontdesk/api/{provider}/`
4. **Register in router** in `frontdesk-widget.tsx`
5. **Add navigation** in sidebar component

## 📦 State Management Rules

### Atom Naming Convention
**Pattern**: `frontdesk.{provider}.{data}`

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
frontdesk.internal.conversations
frontdesk.email.accounts
frontdesk.tickets.selectedTicketId
frontdesk.chatwoot.conversations

// ❌ WRONG
internalConversations
emailAccountState
ticketId
```

### State Organization
```typescript
// One atom per data domain
export const emailAccountsAtom = atom<EmailAccount[]>({
  key: 'frontdesk.email.accounts',
  default: []
});

export const emailSelectedAccountIdAtom = atom<string | null>({
  key: 'frontdesk.email.selectedAccountId',
  default: null
});

// Use selectors for derived state
export const emailSelectedAccountSelector = selector({
  key: 'frontdesk.email.selectedAccount',
  get: ({ get }) => {
    const accounts = get(emailAccountsAtom);
    const selectedId = get(emailSelectedAccountIdAtom);
    return accounts.find(a => a.id === selectedId);
  }
});
```

### State Best Practices
1. **Use Recoil for shared state** across components
2. **Use useState for local UI state** (form inputs, modals, etc.)
3. **Normalize data** - avoid duplication in atoms
4. **Use selectors** for computed/derived state
5. **Update atomically** - batch related state updates

## 🌐 Service Layer Rules

### Service Import Pattern
**ALWAYS** use the unified import from `@/services/frontdesk`:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Single unified import
import {
  messagingService,       // WebSocket for DMs
  ticketSocketService,    // WebSocket for Tickets
  directMessagesService,  // REST API for DMs
  ticketsService,         // REST API for Tickets
  chatwootService         // REST API for Chatwoot
} from '@/services/frontdesk';

// ❌ WRONG - Direct imports
import { messagingService } from '@/services/frontdesk/websocket/messaging-service';
```

### Service Implementation Pattern
```typescript
// src/services/frontdesk/api/{provider}/{provider}.service.ts
import { httpClient } from '@/services/frontdesk/http-client';

export class MyProviderService {
  private baseUrl = '/api/v1/my-provider';

  async getItems(filters?: FilterParams): Promise<Item[]> {
    const response = await httpClient.get<Item[]>(this.baseUrl, { params: filters });
    return response.data;
  }

  async getItem(id: string): Promise<Item> {
    const response = await httpClient.get<Item>(`${this.baseUrl}/${id}`);
    return response.data;
  }

  async createItem(data: CreateItemDto): Promise<Item> {
    const response = await httpClient.post<Item>(this.baseUrl, data);
    return response.data;
  }

  async updateItem(id: string, data: UpdateItemDto): Promise<Item> {
    const response = await httpClient.patch<Item>(`${this.baseUrl}/${id}`, data);
    return response.data;
  }

  async deleteItem(id: string): Promise<void> {
    await httpClient.delete(`${this.baseUrl}/${id}`);
  }
}

export const myProviderService = new MyProviderService();
```

## 🎨 Component Patterns

### Standard Component Structure
```typescript
import React, { useCallback, useMemo } from 'react';
import { useRecoilValue } from 'recoil';
import { Box, Typography } from '@mui/material';
import { useMyProvider } from '../hooks/use-my-provider';

interface MyComponentProps {
  // Props interface
}

export const MyComponent: React.FC<MyComponentProps> = ({ ...props }) => {
  // 1. Hooks (Recoil, custom hooks)
  const { data, loading, error } = useMyProvider();

  // 2. Memoized derived state
  const filteredData = useMemo(() => 
    data.filter(item => item.active),
    [data]
  );

  // 3. Memoized callbacks
  const handleClick = useCallback((id: string) => {
    // Handle click
  }, []);

  // 4. Early returns
  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
  if (error) return <div>Error: {error.message}</div>;
  if (!data.length) return <div>No data</div>;

  // 5. Main render
  return (
    <Box>
      <Typography variant="h6">My Component</Typography>
      {filteredData.map(item => (
        <div key={item.id} onClick={() => handleClick(item.id)}>
          {item.name}
        </div>
      ))}
    </Box>
  );
};
```

### Hook Pattern
```typescript
import { useCallback, useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import { useRecoilState } from 'recoil';
import { myProviderService } from '@/services/frontdesk';
import { myDataAtom } from '@/store/frontdesk/atoms/my-provider.atoms';

export const useMyProvider = () => {
  const [data, setData] = useRecoilState(myDataAtom);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
  const [error, setError] = useState<Error | null>(null);

  const fetchData = useCallback(async () => {
    setLoading(true);
    setError(null);
    try {
      const result = await myProviderService.getItems();
      setData(result);
    } catch (err) {
      setError(err as Error);
    } finally {
      setLoading(false);
    }
  }, [setData]);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchData();
  }, [fetchData]);

  const createItem = useCallback(async (data: CreateItemDto) => {
    try {
      const newItem = await myProviderService.createItem(data);
      setData(prev => [...prev, newItem]);
      return newItem;
    } catch (err) {
      throw err;
    }
  }, [setData]);

  return {
    data,
    loading,
    error,
    refresh: fetchData,
    createItem
  };
};
```

## 🔄 Real-Time Updates

### WebSocket Pattern
For providers with real-time updates (DMs, Tickets):

```typescript
// In hook
useEffect(() => {
  if (!conversationId) return;

  // Subscribe to events
  const handleNewMessage = (message: Message) => {
    setMessages(prev => [...prev, message]);
  };

  messagingService.on('message:new', handleNewMessage);

  // Cleanup
  return () => {
    messagingService.off('message:new', handleNewMessage);
  };
}, [conversationId]);
```

### Optimistic Updates Pattern
```typescript
const sendMessage = async (content: string) => {
  const tempId = `temp-${Date.now()}`;
  
  // 1. Update UI immediately (optimistic)
  setMessages(prev => [...prev, {
    id: tempId,
    content,
    status: 'pending',
    timestamp: new Date()
  }]);

  try {
    // 2. Make API call
    const message = await myProviderService.sendMessage(content);
    
    // 3. Replace temp message with real message
    setMessages(prev => prev.map(m => 
      m.id === tempId ? message : m
    ));
  } catch (error) {
    // 4. Remove temp message on failure
    setMessages(prev => prev.filter(m => m.id !== tempId));
    throw error;
  }
};
```

## 🎯 Routing Pattern

### URL Structure
```
/frontdesk?channel={provider}&view={view}&conversationId={id}
```

### Router Implementation
```typescript
// In provider view
const searchParams = useSearchParams();
const channel = searchParams.get('channel');
const view = searchParams.get('view');
const conversationId = searchParams.get('conversationId');

// Navigate programmatically
const router = useRouter();
router.push(`/frontdesk?channel=email&view=inbox&conversationId=${id}`);
```

## 🔍 Common Patterns

### Loading States
```typescript
if (loading) {
  return <LoadingSpinner />;
}
```

### Error States
```typescript
if (error) {
  return (
    <ErrorMessage 
      message={error.message}
      onRetry={refresh}
    />
  );
}
```

### Empty States
```typescript
if (!data || data.length === 0) {
  return (
    <EmptyState 
      message="No conversations found"
      action={<Button onClick={handleCreate}>Start Conversation</Button>}
    />
  );
}
```

### Pagination
```typescript
const [page, setPage] = useState(1);
const [hasMore, setHasMore] = useState(true);

const loadMore = useCallback(async () => {
  const nextPage = page + 1;
  const result = await service.getItems({ page: nextPage });
  
  setData(prev => [...prev, ...result.data]);
  setHasMore(result.hasMore);
  setPage(nextPage);
}, [page]);
```

## 🚫 What NOT to Do

1. **Never modify shared components** without approval
2. **Never use provider-specific logic** in shared components
3. **Never skip error handling** in async operations
4. **Never hardcode API URLs** - use service layer
5. **Never put business logic** in components - use hooks
6. **Never use inline styles** - use MUI theme/sx prop
7. **Never skip loading states** - always show loading UI

